**=================================================================================================
** TIE CONSTRAINTS (Abaqus *TIE, TYPE=SURFACE TO SURFACE -> EdelweissFE type=tie)
**=================================================================================================
** first-listed surface is the slave (matches the source model's own convention)

*constraint, name=tieNutToAnchor, type=tie
slaveSurface=anchor_to_nut_facets, masterSurface=nut_to_anchor_facets

** POSITION TOLERANCE=0.6 in the source model: covers the DIN 125 clearance bore gap between the
** washer's inner bore and the nut's bottom radius (see AnchorPryOut.inp comment)
*constraint, name=tieNutToWasher, type=tie
slaveSurface=nut_to_washer_facets, masterSurface=washer_to_nut_facets, positionTolerance=0.6

*constraint, name=tieWasherToPlate, type=tie
slaveSurface=washer_bottom_facets, masterSurface=plate_top_facets

*constraint, name=tieAnchorToMortar, type=tie
slaveSurface=mortar_to_anchor_facets, masterSurface=anchor_to_mortar_facets

** Full bond length: concrete_to_mortar (the concrete borehole wall) and mortar_to_concrete (the
** mortar solid's outer face) both now span the same 80 mm embedment depth (see header point 7 --
** the borehole used to erroneously extend the full 240 mm slab height before a Cubit geometry
** fix). All 373 slave nodes tie (0 untied); no explicit positionTolerance needed, the default
** (positionToleranceFactor=0.25 times mortar_to_concrete's mean facet size) covers the sub-mm
** mesh-discretization gap comfortably on its own.
*constraint, name=tieMortarToConcrete, type=tie
slaveSurface=concrete_to_mortar_facets, masterSurface=mortar_to_concrete_facets

**=================================================================================================
** CONTACT (Abaqus General Contact, linear pressure-overclosure -> penalty=1e6, type=linear)
**=================================================================================================
** plate/concrete bearing surface: Abaqus SMALL SLIDING -> sliding=small
*constraint, name=contactPlateConcrete, type=nodeToDeformableSurfacePenalty
slaveSurface=plate_bottom_facets, masterSurface=concrete_top_facets, penalty=1e5, sliding=small, type=quadratic

** anchor shaft / plate hole: Abaqus FINITE SLIDING -> sliding=finite (EdelweissFE default)
*constraint, name=contactShaftHole, type=nodeToDeformableSurfacePenalty
slaveSurface=anchor_to_plate_facets, masterSurface=plate_to_anchor_facets, penalty=1e5, sliding=small, type=quadratic

**=================================================================================================
** INITIAL MESH REFINEMENT (h-adaptivity) -- a feature Abaqus doesn't have
**=================================================================================================
** One-time (initialOnly), geometry-driven refinement of the concrete elements touching the
** borehole wall (the concrete_to_mortar surface -- also tieMortarToConcrete's slave surface),
** exercising the tie's reconcile() on the fully-bonded borehole tie under refinement. refineElSet
** restricts the AMR octree to the "concrete" elset (the only hex20-family elset in this model
** anyway, so this is belt-and-suspenders). maxLevel=1/splitFactor=2 (defaults): each marked
** element splits into 8 children once. Verified (see conversation history): after refinement the
** tie still ties every node correctly (tied count grows with the finer mesh, untied stays 0).
*modelModifier, type=hAdaptivity, name=amrConcreteBorehole
>>marker, type=surface, surface=concrete_to_mortar, initialOnly=True
** >>marker, type=fieldOutput, fieldOutput=alphaPForAMR, expression='abs(x) > 1.0'
>>marker, type=fieldOutput, fieldOutput=stressForAMR, operator='>=', threshold=2.10
refineElSet=concrete
maxLevel=1
splitFactor=3
minMarkedElements=10

**=================================================================================================
** JOB / SOLVER
**=================================================================================================
*job, name=anchorPryOut, domain=3d
*solver, solver=NISTParallel, name=theSolver
linsolver=blockamg
linsolverConfigFile=blockamg.json

**=================================================================================================
** FIELD OUTPUTS
**=================================================================================================
*fieldOutput
>>perElement, name=alphaP, elSet=concrete, result=alphaP, quadraturePoint=0:8, f(x)='np.max(x,axis=1)'
>>perElement, name=damage, elSet=concrete, result=omega, quadraturePoint=0:8, f(x)='np.max(x,axis=1)'
>>perNode, name=displacement, elSet=all, field=displacement, result=U
>>perNode, name=nonlocalDamage, elSet=concrete, field=nonlocal damage, result=U
>>perNode, name=RF_loading, nSet=plate_left_loading, field=displacement, result=P, f(x)='np.sum(x[:,0])', saveHistory=True
>>perNode, name=U_loading, nSet=plate_left_loading, field=displacement, result=U, f(x)='np.mean(x[:,0])', saveHistory=True
>>perElement, elSet=concrete, name=stressForAMR, result=stress, quadraturePoint=0:8, f(x)='eigVal(x.reshape(-1,6))[:,0].reshape(x.shape[0],x.shape[1])'

*output, type=ensight, name=esExport
>>perNode, fieldOutput=displacement
>>perNode, fieldOutput=nonlocalDamage
>>perElement, fieldOutput=damage
>>perElement, fieldOutput=alphaP
>>configuration, overwrite=yes

*output, type=monitor, name=monitor
fieldOutput=RF_loading
fieldOutput=U_loading

**=================================================================================================
** STEPS
**=================================================================================================
** Step 1 ("zero" in the source model): trivial warm-up step at zero load, establishing consistent
** tie/contact state before loading (mirrors the source model's zero-length *Static warm-up step).
*step, solver=theSolver
maxInc=1, minInc=1, maxNumInc=1, maxIter=25, stepLength=1
>>dirichlet, name=fixLeft,        nSet=left,           field=displacement, 1=0, 2=0, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=fixRight,       nSet=right,          field=displacement, 1=0, 2=0, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=fixBack,        nSet=back,           field=displacement, 1=0, 2=0, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=fixBottom,      nSet=bottom,         field=displacement, 1=0, 2=0, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=zSymmConcrete,  nSet=z_symm_concrete_free, field=displacement, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=zSymmSteel,     nSet=z_symm_steel_free,    field=displacement, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=plateXFix,      nSet=plate_left_loading, field=displacement, 1=0

** Step 2 ("loading" in the source model): ramp the plate's x-displacement to 5.0 mm using an
** Abaqus SMOOTH STEP-equivalent amplitude (quintic smoothstep, zero slope/curvature at both ends).
** Increment control mirrors the source model's *Dynamic data line (5e-3, 1, 1e-08, 5e-3).
*step, solver=theSolver
maxInc=5e-3, minInc=1e-8, maxNumInc=100000, maxIter=25, criticalIter=10, stepLength=1
>>options, name=theSolver, extrapolation=linear, useAmgclMPCCondensation=True
>>dirichlet, name=fixLeft,        nSet=left,           field=displacement, 1=0, 2=0, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=fixRight,       nSet=right,          field=displacement, 1=0, 2=0, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=fixBack,        nSet=back,           field=displacement, 1=0, 2=0, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=fixBottom,      nSet=bottom,         field=displacement, 1=0, 2=0, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=zSymmConcrete,  nSet=z_symm_concrete_free, field=displacement, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=zSymmSteel,     nSet=z_symm_steel_free,    field=displacement, 3=0
>>dirichlet, name=plateXFix,      nSet=plate_left_loading, field=displacement, 1=5.0
